# CRUD Server Patterns (apps/crud)

## Server Initialization

Boot sequence: DB ping → `createApp()` → Express listen. Never skip the DB ping.

```ts
// src/index.ts
async function start() {
  await db.execute(sql`SELECT 1`)          // verify DB before serving traffic
  const server = createApp()
  await new Promise<void>((r) => server.once("listening", r))
  console.log(`✓ [server] http://localhost:${port}`)
}
```

## Routes

- One router file per resource in `src/routes/`
- Always `router.use(is_authenticated)` as first line (or `verify_token` for routes that predate user creation like `/auth/sync`)
- Export as `*_router` named export
- Mount in `src/app.ts` only

```ts
// src/routes/exam.ts
const router: IRouter = Router()
router.use(is_authenticated)

router.get("/", get_exams)
router.post("/", create_exam)
router.get("/:id", get_exam)
router.put("/:id", update_exam)
router.delete("/:id", delete_exam)
router.patch("/:id/bookmark", toggle_exam_bookmark)

export { router as exam_router }
```

## Controllers

- One file per action in `src/controllers/<resource>/` (e.g. `create-exam.ts`, `get-exams.ts`)
- Zod schema declared at the bottom of the file, named `z_<action>_body` / `z_<action>_query`
- Parse request at the top — Zod throws on invalid input → caught by `error_handler`
- Access user via `req.user!` — always guarded by middleware
- Use `throw_error(code, message)` for business-logic errors; never `res.status().json()` for errors
- Return `{ message, data }` on success

```ts
// src/controllers/exam/create-exam.ts
export const create_exam = async (req: Request, res: Response): Promise<void> => {
  const { title, description, duration_mins } = z_create_exam_body.parse(req.body)
  if (!req.user) throw_error(401, "User not authenticated")

  const row = await db
    .insert(exams)
    .values({ title, description, created_by: req.user!.id, duration_mins })
    .returning()

  res.status(201).json({ message: "Exam created successfully", data: row[0] })
}

const z_create_exam_body = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1),
  description: z.string().optional(),
  duration_mins: z.number().min(1),
})
```

**List/filter controllers** — use `and()` + conditional clauses; run count + data in parallel:

```ts
export const get_exams = async (req: Request, res: Response) => {
  const { page, limit, search } = z_get_exams_query.parse(req.query)
  const { id: user_id, role } = req.user!

  const where = and(
    role !== "admin" ? eq(exams.created_by, user_id) : undefined,
    search ? ilike(exams.title, `%${search}%`) : undefined,
    isNull(exams.deleted_at),
  )

  const [rows, [{ count }]] = await Promise.all([
    db.select().from(exams).where(where).limit(limit).offset((page - 1) * limit),
    db.select({ count: sql<number>`count(*)` }).from(exams).where(where),
  ])

  res.json({ message: "Exams fetched", data: rows, pagination: { total: count, page, limit } })
}
```

## Middleware

- **`is_authenticated`** — verifies Firebase token + loads user from DB → `req.user`
- **`verify_token`** — verifies Firebase token only (no DB lookup) → `req.firebase_user`; use only for routes that run before user exists in DB (e.g. `/auth/sync`)
- **`is_admin`** — same as `is_authenticated` + checks `user.role === "admin"` → 403 otherwise
- Auth failures return `{ error: string, code: number }` (not `message`)

```ts
// is_authenticated pattern
const decoded = await auth.verifyIdToken(token)
const user = await db.select().from(users).where(eq(users.firebase_uid, decoded.uid)).then(r => r[0])
if (!user) { res.status(401).json({ error: "User not found", code: 401 }); return }
req.user = user
next()
```

## Drizzle ORM

- Schema is in `packages/db/src/schema/` — never define tables inside `apps/crud`
- Import tables from `@examhell/db`
- DB client: `export const db = createDb(env.DATABASE_URL)` in `src/db/index.ts`
- Soft deletes via `deleted_at` timestamp — filter with `isNull(table.deleted_at)` in queries
- Use `.returning()` on `insert`/`update` to get back the row in one round-trip

```ts
// Always import schema from the package
import { exams, users } from "@examhell/db"
```

## Error Handling

```ts
// throw_error for business logic
throw_error(404, "Exam not found")      // throws AppError(404, msg)
throw_error(403, "Forbidden")

// error_handler in app.ts catches:
// - AppError         → { message, data: null } with the given code
// - ZodError         → 400 { message, data: null }
// - PG unique error  → 409
// - fallthrough      → 500
```

## Type Augmentation

`req.user` and `req.firebase_user` are declared in `src/types/express.d.ts` — never cast `req` to `any`.

```ts
// types/express.d.ts pattern
declare global {
  namespace Express {
    interface Request {
      user?: TUser
      firebase_user?: TFirebaseUser
    }
  }
}
```
